MID_EV12_040_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_040_m01_001: I observed your battle the other day—another\nstriking display of your strength.
MID_EV12_040_m01_002: You can now advance to the main matches. And so I\nmust offer you sincere congratulations.
MID_EV12_040_m01_003: You summoned me for this?
MID_EV12_040_m01_004: Though I suspected it would not please you, I must\nabide by due formality.
MID_EV12_040_m01_005: In truth, I do have one question I neglected to ask\nyou before.
MID_EV12_040_m01_006: If you would, I would like to hear what it is you\ndesire should you triumph in the Heroic Games.
MID_EV12_040_m01_007: <NCA>Mention Dagda's warships.
MID_EV12_040_m01_008: <NCB>Mention Cetus, the Sea Tyrant.
MID_EV12_040_m01_009: <ACA>I ask only you grant me one of Dagsion's warships.
MID_EV12_040_m01_010: <ACA>Oh. This, I had not foreseen.
MID_EV12_040_m01_011: <ACA>It is true that Dagsion berths powerful warships,\nuntouched for hundreds of years.
MID_EV12_040_m01_012: <ACA>What are your intentions? I would hear of your plans.
MID_EV12_040_m01_013: I desire to fight a monster I encountered earlier—\nCetus, the Sea Tyrant.
MID_EV12_040_m01_014: Oh?
MID_EV12_040_m01_015: I have been told that Dagdan warships\nare unsinkable.
MID_EV12_040_m01_016: If there is one ship that could withstand Cetus's rage,\nit would be yours.
MID_EV12_040_m01_017: I have heard rumors of this Sea Tyrant. It is said that\nthe creature is a threat to all seafarers.
MID_EV12_040_m01_018: Rumor would have it that many of those lost on the\nLir Sea are in fact Cetus's victims.
MID_EV12_040_m01_019: There will come a day when the empire can no\nlonger ignore this threat.
MID_EV12_040_m01_020: It may be that adding a warship to your arsenal of\nstrength and blade would assure your victory.
MID_EV12_040_m01_021: Perhaps. It would be interesting, certainly.
MID_EV12_040_m01_022: If you plan to slay the beast, a ship shall be yours.\nWith all haste.
MID_EV12_040_m01_023: Truly?
MID_EV12_040_m01_024: The elimination of the Sea Tyrant would be a boon\nto the empire.
MID_EV12_040_m01_025: You must understand, though, that our warships are\nmassive. It takes a thousand men to crew just one.
MID_EV12_040_m01_026: And they have been berthed for more than five\nhundred years... Surely they are in need of repair.
MID_EV12_040_m01_027: It will take some time before we have a seaworthy\nvessel readied for you. So please, be patient.
MID_EV12_040_m01_028: But it is gladly given. We will begin the preparations.
MID_EV12_104_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_104_m01_001: My blade sings. Tell me, Answerer...
MID_EV12_104_m01_002: This sound...I have never heard it before. Could it be\nyou?
MID_EV12_104_m01_003: Father, what is it?
MID_EV12_104_m01_004: Can this mean that you do covet his body?
MID_EV12_104_m01_005: *gasp*
MID_EV12_104_m01_006: Hehehe! The moment I've been waiting for, ever\nsince the first time I saw your little gem.
MID_EV12_104_m01_007: Baozi! You dare?
MID_EV12_104_m01_008: Just one look tells you it's worth a bundle.
MID_EV12_104_m01_009: But it's not just pretty, is it? You ladies actually\nworship the thing.
MID_EV12_104_m01_010: Can't say I understand, but who cares? Just call it a\nthank-you for my hard work.
MID_EV12_104_m01_011: You abhorrent pig! That is not for the likes of you\nto touch!
MID_EV12_104_m01_012: Whoa, now! If you want to hang on to it, you'll have\nto do what I tell you.
MID_EV12_104_m01_013: Esteemed Magistra—take off that mask.
MID_EV12_104_m01_014: Rrgh. If I must.
MID_EV12_104_m01_015: Hah hah hah! Turns out you're gorgeous! I knew it!
MID_EV12_104_m01_016: You had me fooled, but not anymore. In fact, maybe\nit's time I took control.
MID_EV12_104_m01_017: You've been pushing me around for so long... I think\nit's time for some payback.
MID_EV12_104_m01_018: Ngh!
MID_EV12_104_m01_019: What do you think you're doing?
MID_EV12_104_m01_020: It would seem that beauty is something you lack.
MID_EV12_104_m01_021: You two are ill-matched. I will duel you instead.
MID_EV12_041_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_041_m01_001: At last we set sail. I find I must commend Dagda the\nGreat's warships.
MID_EV12_041_m01_002: I have never before laid eyes on a wooden ship of\nsuch inordinate scale.
MID_EV12_041_m01_003: It is five hundred years old though. It's no surprise\nthat it's a little...behind the times.
MID_EV12_041_m01_004: Yet the fact that the whole thing is made from\nguibouga... The cost! I can't even imagine it.
MID_EV12_041_m01_005: Dagda the Great certainly had his moments, didn't\nhe? Thanks to that, we have this sturdy ship.
MID_EV12_041_m01_006: This thing might actually stand up to the Sea\nTyrant after all.
MID_EV12_041_m01_007: I've never been on a warship before. Sweetie, have\nyou SEEN the oar deck?
MID_EV12_041_m01_008: <NCA>Allow that you have not.
MID_EV12_041_m01_009: <NCB>Say that you have.
MID_EV12_041_m01_010: <ACA>Not yet.
MID_EV12_041_m01_011: <ACA>What? We have to go check it out!
MID_EV12_041_m01_012: <ACB>I have, yes.
MID_EV12_041_m01_013: <ACB>Amazing, right? I've never seen anything like it.
MID_EV12_041_m01_014: There are hundreds of people, all rowing in time to\nthe beat of a drum!
MID_EV12_041_m01_015: I couldn't believe my eyes! I've been buzzing nonstop\never since.
MID_EV12_041_m01_016: I know my way around a boat, but...nothing like this.\nThis is just beyond.
MID_EV12_041_m01_017: A tiny fishing boat would hardly compare to this, I\nshould think.
MID_EV12_041_m01_018: Anyway, Fabio, what's the plan?
MID_EV12_041_m01_019: Ah, yes. I have considered the matter and prepared\na course of action. We are now in Dagsion.
MID_EV12_041_m01_020: We will head north from Lake Baal and continue\nalong the Talto River.
MID_EV12_041_m01_021: Once we cross the floodgates of Fort Galcar, we will\narrive at the river mouth and head into Pasha Bay.
MID_EV12_041_m01_022: From there, we will advance due west across the\nLir Sea.
MID_EV12_041_m01_023: We will search the waters where Dietrich first\ncaught sight of Cetus, the Sea Tyrant.
MID_EV12_041_m01_024: As we will be sailing against both the current and\nthe seasonal winds, the rowers will be tested.
MID_EV12_041_m01_025: Soon, we will meet again. How long I have waited.
MID_EV12_041_m01_026: Our course is laid. I will exert my full strength to\nyour goal.
MID_EV12_041_m01_027: Sounds like we have a long way to go.\nAnybody hungry?
MID_EV12_041_m01_028: A ship this big must have somewhere I can cook.
MID_EV12_041_m01_029: After dinner, I'll make us all coffee. I brew a lovely\ncup. How does that sound?
MID_EV12_042_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_042_m01_001: The ship's rocking, and it's gloomy out. Don't like\nthat much.
MID_EV12_042_m01_002: No, it's not good. The wind is strong, the air is heavy,\nand the water's choppy.
MID_EV12_042_m01_003: We should have the rowers pull back their oars while\nwe ride out the storm.
MID_EV12_042_m01_004: Otherwise, they might snap. You there—tell\nthe captain!
MID_EV12_042_m01_005: Upon the sea, you have a completely different air.
MID_EV12_042_m01_006: Something wrong, Fabio? You never look good, but\ntoday you look really, really not good.
MID_EV12_042_m01_007: An unpleasant sensation of uncertain origin has\nmade itself known deep inside me.
MID_EV12_042_m01_008: I have lived long, but this...this is unknown to me...
MID_EV12_042_m01_009: Are you serious? You're seasick!
MID_EV12_042_m01_010: Go stand in the middle of the deck and look at the\nhorizon. Whatever you do, don't look down.
MID_EV12_042_m01_011: That I must follow your orders... How vexing.
MID_EV12_042_m01_012: Fabio's right, by the way. I can see how confident\nyou are out here. It's reassuring.
MID_EV12_042_m01_013: My dad taught me everything there is to know\nabout sailing. Navigating, reading the weather...
MID_EV12_042_m01_014: Whether it's a giant warship or a tiny fishing boat,\nnot much changes.
MID_EV12_042_m01_015: Sweetie, how are you holding up? You're not used\nto boats, right?
MID_EV12_042_m01_016: <NCA>Consider.
MID_EV12_042_m01_017: Hmm...
MID_EV12_042_m01_018: That day...the seas were rough.
MID_EV12_042_m01_019: Could it be? Tsiskaridze said that it brings\nthe storm...
MID_EV12_042_m01_020: What's that noise? It's not the storm. It's shrill.
MID_EV12_042_m01_021: Is that coming from your sword, Dietrich?
MID_EV12_042_m01_022: Our meeting is at hand.
MID_EV12_042_m01_023: Look! Beneath the ship! Something's there...and\nit's huge!
MID_EV12_042_m01_024: Heh. Ehehe. Ahaha. Ahahahah!
MID_EV12_042_m01_025: Cetus! I have awaited you!
MID_EV12_042_m01_026: Here it comes! Everybody—grab hold and don't\nlet go!
MID_EV12_043_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_043_m01_001: Well fought, dark warrior who carries the blood\nof Lamine...
MID_EV12_043_m01_002: Kyaah! What? It can SPEAK?!
MID_EV12_043_m01_003: Driven solely by bestial impulse, I plied the seas,\nchallenging all I laid eyes upon.
MID_EV12_043_m01_004: But at long last, my journeys can come...to an end...
MID_EV12_043_m01_005: This spear... It has the same mark as mine!
MID_EV12_043_m01_006: It is no coincidence. They are connected.
MID_EV12_043_m01_007: That beast was once a hero—one not unlike Lamine,\nDietrich's ancestor.
MID_EV12_043_m01_008: <NCA>Inquire further.
MID_EV12_043_m01_009: Then the Sea Tyrant Cetus was also one of the\n10 Elites?
MID_EV12_043_m01_010: Do not assume the stories peddled by the Church of\nSeiros reflect the true history of this world.
MID_EV12_043_m01_011: Anything the church deemed inconvenient to its\nhegemony was rewritten.
MID_EV12_043_m01_012: The warriors granted Heroes' Relics—that is, Crest\nweaponry—numbered many more than 10.
MID_EV12_043_m01_013: Some challenged dragons and succumbed. Others\nfell victim to strife that bred within their ranks.
MID_EV12_043_m01_014: And others, who fought beyond all endurance,\nbeyond all limit...were consumed by their weapons.
MID_EV12_043_m01_015: They became beasts, driven by instinct to fight on.
MID_EV12_043_m01_016: In that blood-soaked age spanning centuries,\nNemesis, the King of Liberation, led his warriors.
MID_EV12_043_m01_017: Those warriors who survived to leave their mark on\nFódlan are called the 10 Elites. This is the real truth.
MID_EV12_043_m01_018: And this is what became of one warrior of Fódlan\nwho was lost to history.
MID_EV12_043_m01_019: Just so. Esmeralda, you bear the same Crest. It may\nbe that you carry the same blood as well.
MID_EV12_043_m01_020: This was my ancestor?
MID_EV12_043_m01_021: That's...a tragedy.
MID_EV12_043_m01_022: Changed into a beast, trapped by this spear, forced to\nwander the seas alone for however long... How sad.
MID_EV12_043_m01_023: I'm glad that we set Cetus free. Whether or not\nwe're related.
MID_EV12_043_m01_024: Esmeralda, what are you doing?
MID_EV12_043_m01_025: We can't make a grave, but at least we can\nreturn the remains to the sea.
MID_EV12_043_m01_026: There we go.
MID_EV12_043_m01_027: I've always loved the sea, ever since I was little.\nWhen things get tough, I watch the waves...
MID_EV12_043_m01_028: I don't know why, but it always calms me.
MID_EV12_043_m01_029: Even when Dad died, it calmed me... And I didn't\nblame the sea for taking him.
MID_EV12_043_m01_030: No, I'd watch the waves go in and out...and I'd tell\nmyself that he had returned to the sea he loved.
MID_EV12_043_m01_031: Cetus must have loved the sea too. I'm sure of it.
MID_EV12_043_m01_032: You have acted admirably.
MID_EV12_043_m01_033: Well! How rare it is to hear you say that.
MID_EV12_043_m01_034: Oh, Sweetie... You're making me blush!
MID_EV12_043_m01_035: To reach beyond your limits... To tumble into\nbeauteous ruination...
MID_EV12_043_m01_036: It may be that one day, Answerer will consume me\nand I, too, will become a beast.
MID_EV12_043_m01_037: And that would be nothing to lament. No—a fitting\nend for one such as I.
MID_EV12_043_m01_038: Ngh...
MID_EV12_043_m01_039: {SetColor=Gray}If I am there at that moment... What could I say?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_044_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_044_m01_001: This spear we got... Can I try using it?
MID_EV12_044_m01_002: <NCA>Allow it.
MID_EV12_044_m01_003: Of course you may.
MID_EV12_044_m01_004: That is Grasitha. Esmeralda, as you bear the Crest of\nBlaiddyd, it must certainly be yours.
MID_EV12_044_m01_005: None but you could draw out its potential.
MID_EV12_044_m01_006: Does that mean that if I do, I'll end up like Cetus\nsomeday?
MID_EV12_044_m01_007: It is not wholly certain, but I do not believe so.
MID_EV12_044_m01_008: So long as you avoid pushing beyond your limit in\nbattle, you should be well.
MID_EV12_044_m01_009: Using it would be the highest tribute you could pay\nher, would it not?
MID_EV12_044_m01_010: Her? Are you saying Cetus was a woman?
MID_EV12_044_m01_011: Fabio, I think you know something about\nmy ancestor.
MID_EV12_044_m01_012: Some events remain shrouded to me, so anything I\nsay should be treated as speculation.
MID_EV12_044_m01_013: That's fine. I want to know. Tell me whatever\nyou can.
MID_EV12_044_m01_014: I knew of a warrior woman in Fódlan called Hedda.
MID_EV12_044_m01_015: She was a famed dragon hunter who bore the same\nCrest as Blaiddyd the Elite and wielded Grasitha.
MID_EV12_044_m01_016: Southern Fódlan was where she stalked her prey—\nuntil one day, she vanished without a trace.
MID_EV12_044_m01_017: Naturally I presumed that a dragon finally got the\nbetter of her.
MID_EV12_044_m01_018: Now, though, I posit that she crossed the sea. A\ndragon did not end Hedda; this spear consumed her.
MID_EV12_044_m01_019: And so she became Cetus, the Sea Tyrant, and\nroamed the waters seeking the blood of the strong.
MID_EV12_044_m01_020: Or something like that. My imagination does run\naway with me so.
MID_EV12_044_m01_021: Wow, that's quite a story. My ancestor, the dragon\nhunter.
MID_EV12_044_m01_022: Once again you make it sound as if you were present\nas the era of legends unfolded.
MID_EV12_044_m01_023: If I told you I had witnessed it all with my own eyes,\nwould you believe me?
MID_EV12_044_m01_024: <NCA>Nod.
MID_EV12_044_m01_025: <NCB>Scoff.
MID_EV12_044_m01_026: <ACA>Having heard these tales many times now...\nI consider no other possibility.
MID_EV12_044_m01_027: <ACA>It gladdens me to hear that you believe the truth.
MID_EV12_044_m01_028: <ACA>I had never guessed that I might form such a\nconnection with a surface dweller.
MID_EV12_044_m01_029: <ACB>It is all a bit much.
MID_EV12_044_m01_030: <ACB>I cannot blame you. What in your experience has\nprepared you to imagine this to be true?
MID_EV12_044_m01_031: <ACB>I have lived for more than three thousand years, you\nmust understand.
MID_EV12_044_m01_032: What is the difference between your existence and\nthat of a god?
MID_EV12_044_m01_033: I am human. Thoroughly and truly human. And I\ntake pride in being human.
MID_EV12_044_m01_034: I do not accept the divinity of these beings who call\nthemselves gods and hold the surface in thrall.
MID_EV12_044_m01_035: Agartha entrusts much of its decision-making to an\nentity known as Vritra.
MID_EV12_044_m01_036: Truth told, even those who lead Agartha do not truly\napprehend Vritra's thoughts.
MID_EV12_044_m01_037: Perhaps I, after all this time, have wearied of that.
MID_EV12_044_m01_038: I consider it my mission to obey the orders of a\ndistant machine whom I scarcely comprehend.
MID_EV12_044_m01_039: Yet I was never plagued by doubt. Until now.
MID_EV12_044_m01_040: Is it the sun? Is it you three? I feel a change...
MID_EV12_044_m01_041: Though I say this to you, I do not intend to abandon\nmy task.
MID_EV12_044_m01_042: I must head to the desert to confirm what I learned\nfrom the Grand Megalith.
MID_EV12_044_m01_043: But not simply to fulfill a mission. I, myself,\nam curious.
MID_EV12_044_m01_044: You will have my aid.
MID_EV12_044_m01_045: Are you quite sure? My objective lies far\nfrom Dagsion.